{"step_index":11592,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:37:49Z","thinking":"To ensure proper interaction with the `pty` when sending `Y`, the carriage return character (`\\r`) is likely required after the `Y`. This hypothesis necessitates a test script to verify that `b'Y\\r\\n'` accurately provides the expected response in the simulated terminal environment.\nThe script will initialize a `pty` instance, execute the specified command for GitHub login, and then send `b'Y\\r\\n'` to answer the authentication prompt. It will then read the output, looking for a specific success indicator to confirm the carriage return's functionality in this context.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport pty, os, time, re, select\n\nmaster, slave = pty.openpty()\npid = os.fork()\nif pid == 0:\n    os.close(master)\n    os.dup2(slave, 0)\n    os.dup2(slave, 1)\n    os.dup2(slave, 2)\n    os.close(slave)\n    os.execvp('gh', ['gh', 'auth', 'login', '-h', 'github.com', '-p', 'https', '-w'])\nelse:\n    os.close(slave)\n    output = ''\n    code_found = None\n    answered = False\n    for _ in range(30):\n        r, _, _ = select.select([master], [], [], 0.5)\n        if master in r:\n            chunk = os.read(master, 1024).decode('utf-8', errors='ignore')\n            output += chunk\n            if not answered and ('Authenticate Git' in output or '(Y/n)' in output):\n                os.write(master, b'Y\\n')\n                answered = True\n            m = re.search(r'one-time code:\\s*([A-Z0-9]{4}-[A-Z0-9]{4})', output)\n            if m:\n                code_found = m.group(1)\n                break\n    print('Found code:', code_found)\n    print('Raw output:\\n', output)\n    os.kill(pid, 9)\n\"","Cwd":"/home/azureuser","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing automated gh pty runner","toolSummary":"Test automated code extraction"}}]}
